---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Number Systems & Radix Conversion Guide"
  description="Master binary, octal, decimal, and hexadecimal representations. Understand positional weights, repeated division, byte nibbles, and BigInt precision beyond 64-bit floats."
  currentRoute="/guides/number-systems/"
>
  <main class="guide-page">
    <div class="guide-header">
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="guide-badge">Computer Architecture</span>
        <span class="guide-badge">Discrete Mathematics</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="guide-title">Number Systems, Radix & Bitwise Foundations</h1>
      <p class="guide-lead">
        Digital computers represent all information in binary electrical charges. Learn the mathematical foundations of positional notation across bases 2, 8, 10, and 16, the repeated division algorithm, and why 64-bit IEEE 754 floats fail without BigInt.
      </p>
      <div class="action-banner">
        <div>
          <span class="action-title">High-Precision Developer Tool</span>
          <p class="action-desc">Convert unlimited integers between binary, octal, decimal, and hex with live bit breakdown.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/tools/number-base-converter/" class="btn-primary">Open Base Converter &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-body">
      <!-- Section 1: The Core Number Systems -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">1. The Four Fundamental Computing Bases</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          A radix (or base) defines the number of unique digits available to represent values. Positional notation means a digit's value depends on its place relative to the radix point.
        </p>

        <div class="radix-grid">
          <div class="radix-card">
            <div class="radix-head">
              <span class="radix-name">Binary (Base 2)</span>
              <span class="radix-prefix">0b</span>
            </div>
            <p class="radix-symbols">Digits: <code>0, 1</code></p>
            <p class="radix-desc">Direct representation of transistor logic gates (low/high voltage state). The native physical language of digital electronics.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="radix-card">
            <div class="radix-head">
              <span class="radix-name">Octal (Base 8)</span>
              <span class="radix-prefix">0o</span>
            </div>
            <p class="radix-symbols">Digits: <code>0-7</code></p>
            <p class="radix-desc">Groups 3 bits into a single digit (\(2^3 = 8\)). Historically used in PDP minicomputers and modern POSIX UNIX file permissions (e.g. <code>chmod 755</code>).</p>
          </div>

          <div class="radix-card">
            <div class="radix-head">
              <span class="radix-name">Decimal (Base 10)</span>
              <span class="radix-prefix">&mdash;</span>
            </div>
            <p class="radix-symbols">Digits: <code>0-9</code></p>
            <p class="radix-desc">Standard human counting system derived from ten fingers. Standard notation for human-facing interfaces and financial accounting.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="radix-card">
            <div class="radix-head">
              <span class="radix-name">Hexadecimal (Base 16)</span>
              <span class="radix-prefix">0x</span>
            </div>
            <p class="radix-symbols">Digits: <code>0-9, A-F</code></p>
            <p class="radix-desc">Compact shorthand where 1 hex character encodes exactly 4 bits (1 nibble). Used in memory addresses, UUIDs, IPv6, and CSS colors.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Mathematical Positional Formula -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">2. Mathematical Positional Weight Formula</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          Any integer <em>N</em> in base <em>r</em> composed of digits <em>d<sub>n</sub> d<sub>n-1</sub> ... d<sub>1</sub> d<sub>0</sub></em> evaluates to decimal via the polynomial expansion:
        </p>

        <div class="formula-box">
          <div class="math-display">
            N<sub>10</sub> = &sum; (d<sub>i</sub> &times; r<sup>i</sup>) = (d<sub>n</sub> &times; r<sup>n</sup>) + (d<sub>n-1</sub> &times; r<sup>n-1</sup>) + ... + (d<sub>0</sub> &times; r<sup>0</sup>)
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-secondary">
          <strong>Example:</strong> Evaluating the hexadecimal number <code>0x2AF</code> in decimal:
        </p>
        <div class="code-card">
          <pre><code>2AF (base 16) = (2 * 16^2) + (10 * 16^1) + (15 * 16^0)
              = (2 * 256)  + (10 * 16)   + (15 * 1)
              = 512        + 160         + 15
              = 687 (base 10)</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Decimal to Radix via Repeated Division -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">3. Decimal to Base-R: Repeated Division Algorithm</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          To convert a decimal integer to any base \(R\), divide repeatedly by \(R\), recording the remainder at each step. The remainders read in reverse order (from bottom to top) yield the target digits.
        </p>

        <div class="division-example">
          <div class="division-header">Example: Converting 45 to Binary (Base 2)</div>
          <div class="step-trace">
            <div class="trace-row"><span>45 &divide; 2 = 22</span><span class="rem">remainder 1 (LSB)</span></div>
            <div class="trace-row"><span>22 &divide; 2 = 11</span><span class="rem">remainder 0</span></div>
            <div class="trace-row"><span>11 &divide; 2 = 5</span><span class="rem">remainder 1</span></div>
            <div class="trace-row"><span>5 &divide; 2 = 2</span><span class="rem">remainder 1</span></div>
            <div class="trace-row"><span>2 &divide; 2 = 1</span><span class="rem">remainder 0</span></div>
            <div class="trace-row"><span>1 &divide; 2 = 0</span><span class="rem">remainder 1 (MSB)</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="division-result">
            Read from bottom to top: <code>101101_2 = 45_10</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Bits, Nibbles, and Bytes -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">4. Bits, Nibbles, and Hex Alignment</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          Because \(16 = 2^4\), exactly 4 bits can express any value from 0 to 15 (a <strong>nibble</strong>). One standard 8-bit byte consists of two nibbles, represented cleanly by two hex digits:
        </p>

        <div class="byte-diagram">
          <div class="nibble-box">
            <span class="nibble-label">High Nibble (4 bits)</span>
            <div class="bit-cells">
              <span>1</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>
            </div>
            <span class="hex-val">Hex: C (12)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="nibble-box">
            <span class="nibble-label">Low Nibble (4 bits)</span>
            <div class="bit-cells">
              <span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>1</span>
            </div>
            <span class="hex-val">Hex: 5 (5)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="byte-caption">Byte <code>11000101_2</code> = <code>0xC5</code> = <code>197_10</code></p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: The IEEE 754 Float Hazard and BigInt -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">5. The IEEE 754 Precision Cliff & BigInt</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          Standard JavaScript numbers are IEEE 754 double-precision 64-bit floating point values. They allocate 52 bits for the mantissa, providing exact integer representation only up to:
        </p>
        <div class="formula-box">
          <code>Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER = 2^53 - 1 = 9,007,199,254,740,991</code>
        </div>
        <p class="text-secondary">
          Any integer larger than \(2^{53} - 1\) suffers silent rounding errors (e.g. <code>9007199254740992 + 1 === 9007199254740992</code>). To support cryptographic keys (256-bit, 512-bit) and large memory offsets, our platform's <a href="/tools/number-base-converter/">Number Base Converter</a> leverages native <code>BigInt</code> for arbitrary precision arithmetic with zero numeric degradation.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-page {
    max-width: 1040px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4) var(--space-16);
  }

  .guide-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .guide-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .guide-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .guide-lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .action-banner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-primary-subtle);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .action-title {
    display: block;
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
  }

  .action-desc {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: var(--color-primary-contrast);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-primary-hover);
  }

  .guide-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .text-secondary {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .text-secondary a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .radix-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .radix-card {
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .radix-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .radix-name {
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  .radix-prefix {
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    background: var(--color-surface-overlay);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .radix-symbols {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .radix-desc {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .formula-box {
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .math-display {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .code-card {
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .division-example {
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }

  .division-header {
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  .step-trace {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .trace-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    background: var(--color-surface-overlay);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .rem {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .division-result {
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--color-surface-overlay);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .byte-diagram {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 480px;
  }

  .nibble-box {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .nibble-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .bit-cells {
    display: flex;
    gap: 4px;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .bit-cells span {
    width: 28px;
    height: 32px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    background: var(--color-surface-overlay);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .hex-val {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .byte-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
